#: ../../../api/pivot_tables.md:1
msgid ""
"A collection of all {class}`PivotTable <xlwings.PivotTable>` objects on the "
"specified sheet:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/pivot_tables.md:1
msgid "Creates a pivot table on the sheet of this collection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/pivot_tables.md:3
msgid ""
"On macOS, only the first pivot table on a sheet can be created; a second one "
"on the same sheet raises `NotImplementedError`. Existing pivot tables can be "
"modified without that restriction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/pivot_tables.md:0
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/main.py:docstring of xlwings.main.PivotTables.add:10
msgid ""
"The source data, either a range including the header row or a :class:`Table "
"<xlwings.main.Table>`. Can be on another sheet. On xlwings Lite, "
"``expand()`` doesn't see values written in the same script until you run "
"``await book.flush()`` followed by ``await sheet.load()``; on xlwings "
"Server, spell out the range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/main.py:docstring of xlwings.main.PivotTables.add:15
msgid ""
"The cell where the top-left corner of the pivot table goes. Must be on the "
"sheet of this collection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/main.py:docstring of xlwings.main.PivotTables.add:17
msgid ""
"Name of the pivot table. Defaults to Excel's standard name, e.g. "
"``\"PivotTable1\"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/main.py:docstring of xlwings.main.PivotTables.add:19
msgid "Field name(s) for the *Rows* area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/main.py:docstring of xlwings.main.PivotTables.add:20
msgid "Field name(s) for the *Columns* area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/main.py:docstring of xlwings.main.PivotTables.add:21
msgid "Field name(s) for the *Filters* area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/main.py:docstring of xlwings.main.PivotTables.add:22
msgid ""
"Field name(s) for the *Values* area. Use a mapping (``{\"Sales\": \"sum\"}"
"``) or ``(field, function)`` tuples to pick the summary function; ``None`` "
"keeps Excel's default. The same field can only be listed twice via tuples, "
"see :meth:`PivotValueFields.add <xlwings.PivotValueFields.add>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xlwings/main.py:docstring of xlwings.main.PivotTables.add:27
msgid "``\"compact\"``, ``\"outline\"`` or ``\"tabular\"``."
msgstr ""

